sing 7.2 points and taking the lead from -10.8 to -18.1. The engine wanted B5, and Black only played B5 two moves later."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "B5 was the engine's own choice and gained 0.2 points, steadying Black on the left after the G4 slip. Black stayed well behind, but the lead stopped sliding away."}, {"turn": 80, "text": "J7 decided the game. The 20k lost 21.3 points with it, and Black's lead jumped from -9.5 to +11.8, where the engine's choice was F9. Black had been behind since the opening and had lost less per move than the 20k, so it only needed one gift of this size."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "All JavaScript run was a recorder that submits the player's named move and saves the raw responses, an inspector that parses the current board into groups, liberties, regions and area, a verifier that replays the actual move history to check captures and ko, and note and file writing. None of it looped over empty points to score candidates or played continuations forward, so every move was chosen by the player.", "stop": false}}